// Appends a label for each directory sgx_depth levels below sgx_dir, written with
// the prefix sgx_prefix and the directory names, skipping one named sgx_skip. A
// directory with no directory in it, shallower than the depth asked for, is
// labelled itself.
sg_expand(string[] sgx_out, string sgx_dir, string sgx_prefix, int sgx_depth, string sgx_skip) {
  string[] sgx_names = sg_subdirs(sgx_dir);
  int sgx_i = 0;
  while(sgx_i < len(sgx_names)) {
    if(sgx_names[sgx_i] != sgx_skip) {
      sg_expand1(sgx_out, sgx_dir, sgx_prefix, sgx_depth, sgx_names[sgx_i]);
    }
    sgx_i = sgx_i + 1;
  }
} return void;
given sg_t_tree ([], (import sg_t_root), "p/", 1, ""):(["p/sub"])
given sg_t_tree ([], (import sg_t_root), "p/", 2, ""):(["p/sub/more"])
given sg_t_tree ([], (import sg_t_root), "p/", 1, "sub"):([])

sg_expand1(string[] sgy_out, string sgy_dir, string sgy_prefix, int sgy_depth, string sgy_name) {
  string sgy_label = sgy_prefix + sgy_name;
  int sgy_n = len(sgy_out);
  if(sgy_depth > 1) {
    sg_expand(sgy_out, path_join(sgy_dir, sgy_name), sgy_label + "/", sgy_depth - 1, "");
  }
} chain (string[] sgy_out, string sgy_dir, string sgy_prefix, int sgy_depth, string sgy_name) {
  if(len(sgy_out) == sgy_n) {
    push(sgy_out, sgy_label);
  }
} return void;
([], "/nonexistent_sg_root", "p/", 2, "x"):(["p/x"])
